{"content":[{"c":["KIDNEY"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of the body parts of sacrificial animals used for offerings to God. The kidneys, along with their fat, were to be burned on the altar (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.29.13","r":"Exod.29.13","rawR":"Exod.29.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.29.13","value":"Exod.29.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 29:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.3.4-15","r":"Lev.3.4-15","rawR":"Lev.3.4-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.3.4-15","value":"Lev.3.4-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 3:4-15"},") and represented the blood that the Israelites were not permitted to eat."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In a more figurative sense the kidneys are thought of as the seat of human emotions (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.21","r":"Ps.73.21","rawR":"Ps.73.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.21","value":"Ps.73.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 73:21"},") and the rational and moral faculties (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.16.7","r":"Ps.16.7","rawR":"Ps.16.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.16.7","value":"Ps.16.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 16:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.12.2","r":"Jer.12.2","rawR":"Jer.12.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.12.2","value":"Jer.12.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 12:2"},"). They are closely associated with the “heart” and “soul,” standing for one’s innermost self-consciousness. The ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," translates the Hebrew word as “mind,” “heart,” and “soul” in several passages."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["As in the OT Jehovah had knowledge of man’s inmost thoughts (e.g., ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.7.9","r":"Ps.7.9","rawR":"Ps.7.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.7.9","value":"Ps.7.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 7:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.26.2","r":"Ps.26.2","rawR":"Ps.26.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.26.2","value":"Ps.26.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.20.12","r":"Jer.20.12","rawR":"Jer.20.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.20.12","value":"Jer.20.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 20:12"},"), so Christ was identified in the book of Revelation as the one who “searches the minds and hearts” (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.2.23","r":"Rev.2.23","rawR":"Rev.2.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.2.23","value":"Rev.2.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 2:23"},"), making an indirect but clear identification of Jesus with Jehovah. This is the only reference to the kidneys in the NT."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Kidney","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 29:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.29.13","rawQueryValue":"Exod.29.13","sourceRefExact":"Exod.29.13"},{"anchorText":"Lv 3:4-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.3.4-15","rawQueryValue":"Lev.3.4-15","sourceRefExact":"Lev.3.4-15"},{"anchorText":"Ps 73:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.73.21","rawQueryValue":"Ps.73.21","sourceRefExact":"Ps.73.21"},{"anchorText":"Ps 16:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.16.7","rawQueryValue":"Ps.16.7","sourceRefExact":"Ps.16.7"},{"anchorText":"Jer 12:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.12.2","rawQueryValue":"Jer.12.2","sourceRefExact":"Jer.12.2"},{"anchorText":"Pss 7:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.7.9","rawQueryValue":"Ps.7.9","sourceRefExact":"Ps.7.9"},{"anchorText":"26:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.26.2","rawQueryValue":"Ps.26.2","sourceRefExact":"Ps.26.2"},{"anchorText":"Jer 20:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.20.12","rawQueryValue":"Jer.20.12","sourceRefExact":"Jer.20.12"},{"anchorText":"Rv 2:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rev.2.23","rawQueryValue":"Rev.2.23","sourceRefExact":"Rev.2.23"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"43bfe9e7368cc7e7196039702610190ff1702645de138d786b6f46f98ba25b3c","sourceItemName":"Kidney","sourceItemOrder":69,"sourceMember":"Articles/K.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Kidney","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Kidney","title":"Kidney","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}